it is hard to believe that it's been  seven years since a dlc dropped for a  battlefield set in modern times  we've seen a lot of rumors about the  next battlefield game supposedly taking  place in the near future and it might  have highly destructible cities massive  weather events huge player counts  murder robots osprey aircraft and a host  of other things  and of course this has people excited  now we can't confirm it at this point  but what we can do is go back to  battlefield 3  4 and bad company 2 all of which are set  in modern times  and see if those rumors are even good or  bad ideas we have confirmed battlefield  announcements coming in june  and more coming from ea play on july  22nd  we also have a release date sometime  around october to december  so make sure to subscribe to the channel  and give us a thumbs up and we'll let  you know as stuff happens alright let's  get into it  let's start with massive destruction  which is a great idea  large scale destruction hasn't always  been in battlefield games it started  with the little pleasures like blowing  up a bridge in battlefield 2.  it then grew over the years as frostbite  engine was developed and  made less janky  going back to play bad company 2  reminded me that it was just the best in  that department like  hands down the destruction was organic  it was everywhere it was usually right  in your face  battlefield 3 on the other hand traded  better looking graphics and larger map  scale for less destruction that meant  the larger environments were full of  plenty of indestructible features  battlefield 4 returned to destruction in  a pretty big way some of it involving  massive spectacle but often it happened  far away from you and it wasn't quite as  exciting as bad company you might have  not even noticed it if you weren't  looking in the right direction  and some apps were less interesting  afterward the giant rockets and leaked  images do look like some kind of map  event or  major objective indicating a possible  return to battlefield 4  style that could mean parts of maps  being destroyed or just a visual  indicator that matches are getting past  a certain phase  what we're hoping is the next  battlefield game can harness more  powerful consoles and pcs to give  players the best of all worlds the  organic destruction of bad company 2 and  the massive scale of battlefield 3 or 4.  now you should know that it's been  confirmed battlefield 6 will be on  previous gen consoles so we don't know  if that will hold it back  at the highest possible level and we've  said this before but if we could start  with a map like  siege of shanghai and end with a map  that looks like battlefield 3's  aftermath dlc  that's the dream so in the destruction  camp we should now talk about extreme  weather events which  could be a pretty bad idea if we're  looking at what's been done already in  battlefield titles extreme weather  events like tornadoes could be  problematic from a pretty large number  of angles and frostbite engine  might not be up to the task for a  preview of that you just need to look at  parasol storm from battlefield 4.  vehicle physics for any kind of boat or  fast-moving ground vehicle in  battlefield 4 was pretty  janky and when waves kicked up boats did  not interact with the water well  it didn't just look visually odd but it  also made aiming kind of difficult  and i can't imagine having a tornado  nearby would help that  then there's player visibility which is  its own constant problem in battlefield  even up through battlefield v out of  title set in modern times battlefield 4  is probably the worst offender though  it's physically hard to see enemy  players against the background on a lot  of maps and you'll often die from  someone standing right in front of you  that you didn't see  i can't imagine bad weather and objects  getting demolished in front of your face  will help that problem  i'm honestly holding out hope the next  battlefield game just makes it easier to  see enemy players  finally just some quality of life stuff  here that surprised me i forgot that you  couldn't cut your parachute in previous  battlefield games and i'm not really  sure how that's gonna work with getting  sucked up in a tornado  alright so murder robots and in your  future setting is probably a great idea  battlefield games are at their best when  players can use tools in ways you don't  expect  and you bet you're the first thing i did  with battlefield 3 was go trolling with  the eod bot the amount of fun you can  have with modern gadgets really  highlighted what was missing from  battlefield 1 and 5.  ending a sniper duel by road killing  your foe with the uav  oh god you can't do this anymore can you  [Music]  even battlefield hardline's grappling  hooks and zip lines just opened up a lot  of possibilities  it's all about bringing back that  sandbox another aspect of future tech is  it allows squads to play together more  easily  i am a die-hard supporter of the tracer  dart in bad company 2 for its ability to  communicate targets to other people in  your squad battlefield 3  also had its own solutions for  communicating targets to your team which  is where we got the really fun javelin  squads from  wow look at that gorgeous  battlefield 6 will hopefully also make  some progress on giving more information  to keep squads together which can be  really hard to do when splitting your  attention between combat objectives and  where your team's heading  in the totally not confirmed leaked  images of the next battlefield game we  see some osprey aircraft  that's exciting because battlefield has  always had a problem with airplanes they  usually just head off into the sky and  do their own thing with  little impact on matches cute complaint  from old battlefield 2 video  but it doesn't often feel like jets  interact with the battle in a meaningful  way  they just do their damage and leave a  trail of butthurt in their wake  because of that issue a lot of the  medium to smaller sized maps only work  with helicopters  because they can interact with the  ground game that's why ospreys are so  exciting because they're a hybrid  airplane helicopter that can perform  both roles  as a plane they can ferry squads across  larger maps quickly as a helicopter they  can stick around and wreck shop on  objectives  it honestly solves one of battlefield's  longest running challenges with jets  which really just work on massive maps  and even then  only with skilled pilots and speaking of  skill pilots huh we need to talk about  controls  [Music]  mavericks re-engaging sir  aircraft controls in particular in  battlefield games are just not up to par  on a number of levels and have an  incredibly steep and unfriendly learning  curve yes people who put in the time to  master them can be god tier and i don't  want to take that away from you  if that's you but as someone who flew  helicopters a lot during matches back in  the day  i was at square one again crashing all  over the place just trying to remember  the basics  and that wasn't even trying to circle  strafe after spending so much time with  call of duty 2019's helicopters there's  just straight up no reason these  controls need to be that complicated at  a base level  there should be an easy default setting  and then the older controls for skilled  players  aircraft could also be very buggy like  constantly getting stuck in the sky box  or how in battlefield 4 if you inverted  aircraft controls the bomb sites didn't  also invert  so you had to play one aircraft both  inverted and non-inverted at the same  time  trying to fly an osprey with battlefield  4 style controls would be kind of a  nightmare for less experienced players  huge player count could be good or bad  it just  kind of depends in a recent investor  call it was confirmed battlefield 6 is  not a next-gen exclusive title  but the next gen consoles will enable  higher player counts the number being  thrown around out there is about 128 but  here's the thing  more players doesn't equal more fun and  boy did battlefield 364 player operation  metro or battlefield 4's operation  locker just remind me of that  it's an absolute show there are those of  you out there who like that mayhem  good on you but from a battlefield  perspective these maps just feel  pointless  players smash into each other with very  little skill or thought process  involved so how do you do more players  right  [Music]  you need purpose-built maps and the king  of this is still bad company 2 where  almost the entire game was built around  and balanced for rush mode that brought  just the right number of players  crashing together in  fun and consistent ways in contrast rush  really did not work in battlefield 4  when placed on large open maps built for  conquest so we're hoping that  battlefield 6 sticks with the good  tradition of purpose-built maps that  means conquest maps should be large with  every objective a set-piece that has  consequences  like older battlefield games if you  capture an area it should lead to  something  control of an airfield a bombardment a  tank spawn no more  caspian border you're capturing this  ditch because  reasons  in contrast rush maps should be  meandering and tell a good story  simply placing more players on existing  maps can go  very wrong high player count also ties  into the need for cross play  which is also a rumor going back to play  older battlefield games isolated on  their platforms or completely dead  was both not surprising and really sad  it can be hard to get a match or a  decent ping when players start to leave  one platform or another to keep the  healthiest communities alive  battlefield 6 needs cross-play and the  more the merrier if they want to add it  to game pass  another interesting angle that i hadn't  thought of until recently is  if these rumors are referring to bots  games have come a long way with bots  they can really improve the immersion of  a game like they did  in titanfall battlefield 2 back in the  day had full-on bot matches that some  people really enjoyed  we are very excited for the release of  the next battlefield game and to see if  any of these leaks and rumors wind up  being true  there are so many other aspects of  battlefield to explore like if hit  registration and hit markers improve  will battlefield ever get a proper  killcam how will classes be used or  changed this time around  the first official reveal is supposed to  be happening soon but in the meantime  head on over to gamespot's youtube page  and check out our history of destruction  in battlefield  alright thanks for watching  [Music]  you

